<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ellen Johnson Sirleaf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ellen Johnson Sirleaf is a Liberian economist and politician who was elected president in 2005, the first elected woman head of state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Taking office in 2006 after the civil wars, she led reconstruction, debt relief and the response to the Ebola epidemic of 2014. She shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 2011 and left office in 2018.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ellen-johnson-sirleaf.jpg" alt="Ellen Johnson Sirleaf" width="309" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PMO Barbados · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ellen_Johnson-Sirleaf_(2022)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
